Require an open connection in socketSelect(), and give a new socket
connection a defined descriptor and input buffer.

in_R_newsock() (src/modules/internet/sockconn.c) allocates the sockconn
struct with malloc() and leaves fd, pstart and pend for sock_open() to
set.  do_sockselect() (src/main/connections.c) read all three without
checking that the connection was open, so socketSelect() on a socket
connection created with open = "", or one whose open() had failed, used
whatever the allocation contained as a file descriptor: a negative
value indexes the fd_set out of bounds in R_SocketWaitMultiple(), a
large one gives "file descriptor is too large for select()", and a
small one waits on an unrelated descriptor of the process.

ASAN fills the first 4 KiB of every new allocation with 0xbe, so here
the descriptor always reads as negative and the sockets target stops on
its first input that selects an unopened connection:

    s <- socketConnection(port = 8083L, open = "")
    socketSelect(list(s), timeout = 0)

Found by an external report rather than by a fuzzer; the sockets target
(harnesses/sockets.c) was written because of it and reaches it at once.

Upstream status: R Bugzilla 19298 (attachment 4041); r-devel/r-svn
PR #475, filed 2026-11-12.  The upstream PR also adds a regression test
to tests/reg-tests-1e.R, left out here so this carry patch does not go
stale with that file.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/connections.c b/src/main/connections.c
index 25b4bd92ec..a3a6d2d2fd 100644
--- a/src/main/connections.c
+++ b/src/main/connections.c
@@ -6916,6 +6916,9 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_sockselect(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP rho)
 	Rconnection conn = getConnection(asInteger(VECTOR_ELT(insock, i)));
 	if (!strcmp(conn->class, "sockconn")) {
 	    Rsockconn scp = conn->private;
+	    /* the descriptor and input buffer are only set up by sock_open() */
+	    if (!conn->isopen)
+		error(_("connection is not open"));
 	    INTEGER(insockfd)[i] = scp->fd;
 	    if (! LOGICAL(write)[i] && scp->pstart < scp->pend) {
 		LOGICAL(val)[i] = TRUE;
diff --git a/src/modules/internet/sockconn.c b/src/modules/internet/sockconn.c
index 6bd0351b9d..6289720211 100644
--- a/src/modules/internet/sockconn.c
+++ b/src/modules/internet/sockconn.c
@@ -251,6 +251,10 @@ Rconnection in_R_newsock(const char *host, int port, int server, int serverfd,
     ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> timeout = timeout;
     ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> serverfd = serverfd;
     ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> options = options;
+    /* no descriptor and nothing buffered until sock_open() */
+    ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> fd = -1;
+    ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> pstart = ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> inbuf;
+    ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> pend = ((Rsockconn)new->private)-> inbuf;
     return new;
 }
 
